{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And He spread.</b> The hands of Moab in the midst of Moab." "<b>The swimmer.</b> Like one who swims (Ezekiel 47:5)." "<b>And He brought low.</b> The pride of Moab." "<b>With the spreading of His hands.</b> It has no parallel [brother], and its meaning is according to its context. The commentators derived it from the root of עֹשֵׂה אֲרֻבּוֹת (2 Kings 7:2), by a far-fetched route."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:09.426081906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}